From f89073ba4c20f8f92d6afac6f77a3c9e19086bec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Itsnatch <kamaumark996@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 13:11:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: automated payday-based debt recoupment with real
 DusuPay collection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Employers configure their real payday (or the system derives it from actual
processed payroll runs once available, which is more reliable than the
onboarding-time guess) and a mobile money number. On payday, employers get a
forced Yes/No prompt to recoup outstanding advance repayments back to admin —
declining or ignoring it blocks their next advance request until resolved.

Confirming triggers a real DusuPay mobile money collection call. Since DusuPay
has no bank-debit collection method for KES/UGX/TZS/RWF, a failed automated
collection falls back to a manual admin flow: confirm a bank transfer was
received into the company's account and apply it the same way the webhook
would have.

Also fixes a pre-existing bug where the webhook handler routed on
`event.startsWith('collection.')`, but DusuPay's real webhook events are
`transaction.completed`/`transaction.failed` — meaning the existing collection
webhook path (wallet top-ups, manual repayment confirmation) may never have
fired correctly in production. Routing now keys off merchant_reference prefix
instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
